    "id": "05",
    "title": "Kinship Caregiver Support Pilot, Six-Month Evaluation",
    "org": "[ORG_1]",
    "author": "[STAFF_2]",
    "authorType": "staff",
    "dateStart": "2026-01-22",
    "pages": 2,
    "text": "KINSHIP CAREGIVER SUPPORT PILOT, SIX-MONTH EVALUATION\n\n\n\nPrepared by [STAFF_2], Director of Programs. 2026-01-22. Covers 2025-07-07 to 2025-12-31.\n\n§1. Pilot description\nKinship is a seven-session group for parents, guardians, grandparents and older siblings raising a young person who is using or waiting for mental health support. Launched July 2025 with $35,000 from [FUNDER_5] and $22,000 from [FUNDER_4]. Delivered evenings, on site, with food and childcare provided.\n\n§2. Delivery\nFour cycles delivered. 48 caregivers registered, 41 attended at least one session, 33 attended five or more. Mean group size 10.3. Two sessions were relocated to a partner church hall because the group room was double-booked with an Anchor make-up session.\n\n§3. Who attended\n32 of 41 attendees were the caregiver of a youth already receiving a Society service. 9 were not, and 7 of those 9 subsequently referred the young person to Bridge. Kinship is functioning as a referral pathway into the Society, which was not a design goal and was not measured for.\n\n§4. Measurement\nThe Society administered an eight-item satisfaction measure. Mean score 27.4 of 32. No outcome measure was administered to caregivers and no measure was administered to the young people whose caregivers attended. The pilot therefore has strong satisfaction data and no outcome data. The evaluation framework was not finalised before delivery began, which is recorded here as a lesson for future pilots.\n\n§5. Qualitative themes from session feedback forms\nCaregivers most often named isolation, not knowing what to say, and difficulty navigating the health system. 18 of 41 named waiting as their primary stressor, specifically waiting for a specialist appointment for the young person. 11 named language, and asked whether the group could run in Tigrinya or Somali.\n\n§6. Cost and continuation\nSix-month cost $38,400 against a $57,000 two-year budget. Funded to March 2027. Continuation past that date is unfunded.",
