    "text": "FINANCIAL SUMMARY FY2025-26 (UNAUDITED)\n\n\n\nPrepared by [STAFF_3], Finance Manager. 2026-04-30. For Board review. Audit scheduled June 2026.\n\n§1. Revenue\n\n| Source | Restriction | FY2024-25 | FY2025-26 |\n------|\n| [FUNDER_1] City of Edmonton FCSS | Restricted, Anchor and Bridge | $398,000 | $412,000 |\n| [FUNDER_2] Alberta Health Services | Restricted, Bridge | $265,000 | $265,000 |\n| [FUNDER_3] United Way | Restricted, Pathfinder | $165,000 | $180,000 |\n| [FUNDER_4] Kettleridge Family Foundation | Restricted, Pathfinder and Kinship | $95,000 | $125,000 |\n| [FUNDER_5] Alberta Blue Cross Built Together | Restricted, Kinship | nil | $35,000 |\n| Canada Summer Jobs | Restricted, wages | $26,100 | $28,400 |\n| School fee-for-service contracts | Unrestricted | $104,500 | $92,000 |\n| Donations, individual and corporate | Unrestricted | $138,600 | $146,300 |\n| Interest and other | Unrestricted | $9,200 | $11,200 |\n| Total revenue | | $1,201,400 | $1,294,900 |\n\nUnrestricted revenue is 19.2 percent of total, down from 21.0 percent. School contract revenue fell $12,500, tracking the six cancelled Anchor groups.\n\n§2. Expenses\n\n| Category | Budget FY2025-26 | Actual FY2025-26 | Variance |\n------|\n| Salaries and benefits | $941,000 | $946,200 | +$5,200 |\n| Occupancy | $126,000 | $128,400 | +$2,400 |\n| Program delivery and materials | $79,000 | $74,800 | -$4,200 |\n| Interpretation and translation | $5,000 | $17,000 | +$12,000, 240% over |\n| Professional development | $14,000 | $9,600 | -$4,400 |\n| Administration and insurance | $57,000 | $58,300 | +$1,300 |\n| Technology and software | $29,000 | $31,500 | +$2,500 |\n| Fundraising | $24,000 | $22,400 | -$1,600 |\n| Total | $1,275,000 | $1,288,200 | +$13,200 |\n\nSurplus $6,700.\n\n§3. Expense by program\n\n| Program | FY2024-25 | FY2025-26 | Share | Unit cost FY2025-26 | Unit cost change |\n---------|\n| Anchor | $415,000 | $438,000 | 34% | $2,047 per participant | +47% |\n| Bridge | $361,000 | $402,000 | 31% | $334 per contact | -21% |\n| Pathfinder | $206,000 | $246,000 | 19% | $1,662 per youth | -23% |\n| Kinship | nil | $71,000 | 6% | $1,732 per caregiver | new |\n| Shared and administration | $212,400 | $131,200 | 10% | | |\n\n§4. Notes to the summary\na. The interpretation overspend was absorbed from unrestricted donations. A budget line of $18,000 is recommended for FY2026-27.\nb. In November 2025 an invoice of $4,180 for group room furniture was coded to the [FUNDER_2] restricted grant. [FUNDER_2] funds are restricted to Bridge direct service. The error was identified during the December reconciliation, reversed on 2025-12-19, and recoded to unrestricted. [FUNDER_2] was notified in writing on 2025-12-22 and confirmed no further action was required. No other coding errors were identified.\nc. The general liability certificate of insurance lapsed on 2026-01-31 and was renewed on 2026-02-14. The Society was uninsured for 14 days. The renewal is now on a calendar reminder held by two staff.\nd. Restricted funding is 80.8 percent of revenue. Three programs are each dependent on a single funder. The Society has 2.4 months of operating reserve against a board-approved target of 3.0 months.\ne. Participant unit costs in this summary are calculated from billing and attendance records and differ from the figures in the program reports. See document 11.",
