    "id": "07",
    "title": "FCSS Community Investment Report, Q2 FY2025-26",
    "org": "[ORG_1]",
    "author": "[STAFF_2]",
    "authorType": "staff",
    "dateStart": "2025-10-24",
    "pages": 2,
    "text": "FCSS COMMUNITY INVESTMENT REPORT, Q2 FY2025-26\n\n\n\nSubmitted by [STAFF_2] to [FUNDER_CONTACT_1] on 2025-10-24. Reporting period 2025-07-01 to 2025-09-30. Submitted three days after the deadline of 2025-10-21.\n\n§1. Contracted outputs and results\n\n| Contracted output | Target, Q2 | Actual, Q2 | Status |\n------|\n| Walk-in counselling contacts | 250 | 289 | Exceeded |\n| Group program sessions delivered | 48 | 32 | Not met |\n| Youth enrolled in group programming | 72 | 51 | Not met |\n| Youth completing a pre-measure | 290 | 301 | Exceeded |\n| Youth completing a post-measure | 145 | 78 | Not met |\n| Community partner engagements | 12 | 14 | Exceeded |\n\n§2. Narrative, outputs not met\nGroup session delivery fell short because two scheduled groups at [SCHOOL_2] were cancelled for under-enrolment at the two-week registration mark. The Society is reviewing recruitment practice with school partners for the winter term.\n\nPost-measure completion fell short. The contracted target assumes a fixed program exit point. The majority of the Society's contacts in this quarter were single-session walk-ins, which have no exit point at which a post-measure can be administered. The Society raised this with the Coordinator by telephone on 2025-09-08 and proposes renegotiating the post-measure target at the FY2026-27 agreement renewal.\n\n§3. Cumulative year to date\nWalk-in contacts 1,180 year to date across Q1 and Q2 per the FCSS counting definition, which includes only contacts with a completed intake form. Group sessions 61. Youth enrolled in group programming 103.\n\n§4. Coordinator response, recorded 2025-11-04\n[FUNDER_CONTACT_1] acknowledged receipt, noted the late submission, and asked the Society to include the post-measure limitation as a formal note in the Q3 report rather than raising it verbally. The Coordinator advised that the post-measure target cannot be varied mid-agreement.\n\n§5. Preparation note, internal, not submitted to funder\nThis report took 31 staff hours to prepare across four people over the nine days before submission. Attendance data was reconciled by hand from three sources: the intake spreadsheet, the counsellor day sheets, and the school sign-in sheets.",
