    "id": "08",
    "title": "Board of Directors Minutes, 2025-09-17",
    "org": "[ORG_1]",
    "author": "[BOARD_2]",
    "authorType": "governance",
    "dateStart": "2025-09-17",
    "pages": 3,
    "text": "BOARD OF DIRECTORS, MINUTES\n\n\n\nNorthbridge Youth Mental Health Society. 2025-09-17, 18:30, on site. Recorded by [BOARD_2].\n\n§1. Present\n[BOARD_1] Chair, [BOARD_2] Treasurer, [BOARD_3], [BOARD_4], four further directors. Regrets: one director. In attendance: [STAFF_1], [STAFF_3] for item 4.\n\n§2. Approval of minutes\nMinutes of 2025-07-16 approved as circulated. Moved [BOARD_3], seconded [BOARD_4]. Carried.\n\n§3. Executive Director report\n[STAFF_1] reported walk-in volume running 38 percent above the prior year at the half-year mark, with staffing unchanged. Two Anchor groups cancelled for under-enrolment in the autumn term. Pathfinder waitlist at 26 youth, mean wait now over nine days. The Executive Director stated that the Society is now turning youth away on Thursday and Friday afternoons and that this is not consistent with the mission statement.\n\n§4. Finance\n[STAFF_3] presented Q1 and Q2 unaudited results. Interpretation spend already at $9,400 against a $5,000 annual budget. Board directed that the overspend be absorbed from unrestricted funds for the current year and properly budgeted in FY2026-27. Operating reserve at 2.6 months against the 3.0 month policy.\n\n§5. Waitlist policy\nThe Board considered a proposal to introduce a formal Pathfinder waitlist policy including a maximum wait target and a contact protocol for youth waiting more than seven days. Discussion noted that a policy which sets a target the Society cannot meet creates its own risk. Motion: that a Pathfinder waitlist policy be developed by the Director of Programs for approval at the November meeting, including a defined outreach protocol for youth waiting beyond seven days. Moved [BOARD_4], seconded [BOARD_3]. Carried unanimously.\n\n§6. Facility\n[STAFF_1] raised the shortage of private counselling space, reporting that sessions had on several occasions been held in non-private areas. [BOARD_1] asked whether this created a privacy exposure. [STAFF_1] confirmed it did. Motion: that management obtain a contractor assessment and estimate for converting the open work area into enclosed counselling rooms, and report to the Board. Moved [BOARD_1], seconded [BOARD_2]. Carried unanimously.\n\n§7. On-call protocol\n[BOARD_4], as Governance Committee chair, noted that the after-hours response protocol was last reviewed in 2021 and does not address contact received by staff on personal devices. Referred to the Governance Committee to return with a revised protocol. Action: [BOARD_4] and [STAFF_4], report to the November meeting.\n\n§8. Next meeting\n2025-11-19.",
