    "id": "09",
    "title": "Board of Directors Minutes, 2026-02-11",
    "org": "[ORG_1]",
    "author": "[BOARD_2]",
    "authorType": "governance",
    "dateStart": "2026-02-11",
    "pages": 3,
    "text": "BOARD OF DIRECTORS, MINUTES\n\n\n\nNorthbridge Youth Mental Health Society. 2026-02-11, 18:30, on site. Recorded by [BOARD_2].\n\n§1. Present\n[BOARD_1] Chair, [BOARD_2], [BOARD_3], [BOARD_4], five further directors. Full board present. In attendance: [STAFF_1], [STAFF_2], [STAFF_3].\n\n§2. Business arising\na. Pathfinder waitlist policy. Draft presented at the November meeting and deferred for revision. Now at 34 youth waiting with a mean wait of 11.6 days. Deferred again to April. [BOARD_4] recorded a concern that the item has been deferred twice while the underlying number has risen.\nb. On-call protocol. Referred to the Governance Committee 2025-09-17. Committee reported that a draft exists but has not been reviewed against the incident of 2025-10-09. Remains open. Action carried forward, target April 2026.\nc. Facility assessment. Completed. Contractor estimate received from [VENDOR_1] on 2026-03-05 in the amount of $148,400 for conversion of the open work area into three enclosed acoustically treated counselling rooms, an accessible washroom upgrade, and a reception privacy screen. Landlord written consent obtained 2026-03-18.\n\n§3. Executive Director report\nWalk-in volume closing the year approximately 41 percent above prior year. Anchor delivered 18 of 24 scheduled groups. Three staff departures in the year to date, all from the Bridge team. [STAFF_1] reported that exit interviews consistently name unpredictable demand and the absence of private space.\n\n§4. Insurance lapse\n[STAFF_3] reported that the general liability certificate lapsed 2026-01-31 and was renewed 2026-02-14, a 14-day gap in coverage. Cause was a renewal notice sent to a former staff member's address. Board recorded the lapse, accepted the corrective control of dual calendar reminders, and directed that all recurring compliance dates be listed in a single register presented annually. Motion carried.\n\n§5. Capital funding strategy\n[STAFF_1] presented the case for a capital application. The renovation and the associated equipment purchase together are estimated at $180,000, comprising the [VENDOR_1] estimate of $148,400 and $31,600 in furniture, acoustic treatment, secure file storage, four laptops, and group room audiovisual equipment. Discussion noted that the Society is Black-led as recorded in the Governance Committee's annual review, that African and Caribbean origin youth are the largest share of participants, and that a federal capital program for Black-led organisations is the strongest available fit. Motion: that management prepare and submit a capital funding application in the amount of $180,000 for the conversion of the workspace and associated equipment, and that the Chair be authorised as the official representative for attestation purposes. Moved [BOARD_1], seconded [BOARD_3]. Carried unanimously.\n\n§6. Program planning FY2026-27\n[STAFF_2] presented the year-end program picture: rising demand in Bridge and Pathfinder, falling delivery in Anchor, and expenditure still weighted to Anchor at 34 percent of program cost. The Board asked management to return in June with a reallocation option and with an assessment of what the Society would lose in outcome evidence if Anchor were reduced.\n\n§7. Next meeting\n2026-04-15.",
