    "id": "11",
    "title": "Internal email thread: reporting reconciliation",
    "org": "[ORG_1]",
    "author": "[STAFF_1], [STAFF_2], [STAFF_3]",
    "authorType": "staff",
    "dateStart": "2026-01-13",
    "pages": 2,
    "text": "INTERNAL EMAIL THREAD: REPORTING RECONCILIATION\n\n\n\nFive messages, 2026-01-13 to 2026-01-19.\n\n§1. 2026-01-13, 15:02. From [STAFF_3] to [STAFF_2].\nSubject: Q3 numbers do not tie\nI am building the Q3 FCSS report and the walk-in number will not reconcile. I have three different figures for the same nine months.\nIntake spreadsheet: 902. Counsellor day sheets: 934. Billing and attendance records, which is what I use for unit cost: 947.\nWhich one am I reporting.\n\n§2. 2026-01-14, 11:18. From [STAFF_2] to [STAFF_3], copy [STAFF_7].\nSubject: RE: Q3 numbers do not tie\nAll three are correct and they are counting different things.\nThe intake spreadsheet only counts a contact once an intake form is completed. FCSS defines a reportable contact that way, so that is the number that goes in the FCSS report.\nThe day sheets count every young person a counsellor sat with, including the ones who came in, talked for twenty minutes and left without giving a name. Those are real contacts and they are the ones I actually care about clinically.\nBilling counts sessions, so a youth seen twice in a day is two.\nSo we are not wrong, we are just reporting a service we do not fully count.\n\n§3. 2026-01-15, 08:47. From [STAFF_3] to [STAFF_2].\nSubject: RE: Q3 numbers do not tie\nThen the annual program report and the financial summary are going to disagree in print again, the same way they did last year. Bridge will show 1,204 in [STAFF_4]'s report, FCSS will show 1,180, and my cost per contact will be built on 1,247.\nAnyone reading both documents will think one of them is wrong.\nSame issue on Pathfinder. The program report will say 148 youth served, the United Way narrative said 151 because it counted three youth who had a first contact but no service plan.\n\n§4. 2026-01-16, 16:30. From [STAFF_2] to [STAFF_3] and [STAFF_1].\nSubject: RE: Q3 numbers do not tie\nProposal for FY2026-27. One counting definition per metric, written down, with the funder definition mapped to it rather than replacing it. So we count once, our way, and we publish a translation for each funder rather than maintaining three parallel truths.\nI would also like every report we produce to state its counting definition in a footnote. It will look pedantic. It will also mean that when a funder asks why two of our documents disagree we have an answer that took ten seconds instead of a day.\n\n§5. 2026-01-19, 07:31. From [STAFF_1] to [STAFF_2], [STAFF_3], [STAFF_7].\nSubject: RE: Q3 numbers do not tie\nApproved, do it for FY2026-27.\nFor my own record, the Q2 report took 31 hours across four people. That is close to a full staff week, four times a year, spent moving numbers between spreadsheets. That is the single largest administrative cost we do not have a line for.",
