    "authorType": "staff",
    "dateStart": "2026-04-02",
    "pages": 2,
    "text": "STAFFING ROSTER AND TURNOVER LOG FY2025-26\n\n\n\nPrepared by [STAFF_1]. 2026-04-02. Contains no compensation data. Personnel file references only.\n\n§1. Roster at 2026-03-31\n\n| Role | Headcount | FTE | Program |\n------|\n| Counsellor | 6 | 5.6 | Bridge (3.4), Anchor (1.2), shared (1.0) |\n| Youth navigator | 4 | 3.4 | Pathfinder |\n| Group facilitator | 2 | 1.6 | Anchor, Kinship |\n| Intake and data coordinator | 1 | 1.0 | Shared |\n| Management and administration | 4 | 2.6 | Shared |\n| Summer students | 2 | 0.0 at year end | Bridge, Pathfinder |\n| Total | 19 | 14.2 | |\n\nFTE is unchanged from FY2024-25 across every program.\n\n§2. Departures\n\n| Date | Role | Program | Tenure | Reason recorded | Exit interview held |\n---------|\n| 2025-08-22 | Counsellor | Bridge | 2 yr 4 mo | Resigned, moved to AHS position | Yes |\n| 2025-11-28 | Counsellor | Bridge | 1 yr 1 mo | Resigned, no onward role stated | Yes |\n| 2026-01-16 | Counsellor | Bridge | 3 yr 7 mo | Resigned, moved to private practice | Yes |\n| 2026-02-27 | Group facilitator | Anchor | 8 mo | End of term contract, not renewed | No |\n\nTurnover 21 percent (4 of 19). Bridge team turnover 50 percent (3 of 6 counsellor positions).\n\n§3. Exit interview themes, three interviews\nThree of three named unpredictable daily demand and the inability to plan a day. Three of three named the absence of consistent private space, with one describing having conducted a session in the reception area. Two of three named caseload volume. Two of three explicitly stated they were not leaving because of the team or the management. One named compensation. None named the youth or the work itself.\n\n§4. Recruitment\nTwo counsellor positions were posted. Time to fill 11 weeks and 14 weeks. One position was vacant for the whole of February 2026. Coverage during vacancies was absorbed by existing staff, which is not recorded anywhere as a cost.\n\n§5. Credentials and compliance\nProfessional registration is verified at hire and annually thereafter. At the 2026-03-31 check, two of six counsellors did not have a current-year registration confirmation on file. Both were confirmed as registered and in good standing by direct verification on 2026-04-01, and the file copies were obtained the same day. The annual verification is currently a manual task with no reminder attached to it.\n\n§6. Professional development\nBudget $14,000, spend $9,600. Underspend of $4,400 in a year with 21 percent turnover. Three staff did not take any professional development. All three cited coverage.",
